  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "All evidence molecules with numeric absolute or reported oral bioavailability values in ordinary adult/patient conditions exceed 20%, with most values between 49% and 100%. The only sub-20% values are population-specific indomethacin records in preterm/newborn infants, which are outweighed by adult absolute bioavailability data. Therefore, the query is predicted to have high oral bioavailability at the F >= 20% threshold.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "Indomethacin has low oral bioavailability values (13–20%) in preterm/newborn infants, but these are population-specific and less transferable than adult absolute F measurements.",
    "Some records use qualitative terms or unspecified bioavailability report types; numeric absolute F measurements were prioritized."
  ],
